generator_misuse.vlt:4:11: error: a generator must declare its return type
TypeScript allows this (it infers `Generator<T, void, unknown>`); Velt doesn't because the type of the values a generator yields is part of its signature, which is not inferred from its body; write `Generator<T>`, where `T` is the type of the values it yields
generator_misuse.vlt:8:21: error: the return type of a generator must be `Generator<T>`, `Iterator<T>` or `Iterable<T>`, found `i64[]`
write `Generator<T>`, where `T` is the type of the values it yields (`Generator<i64[]>` if it yields `i64[]` values)
generator_misuse.vlt:14:10: error: a generator cannot return a value
TypeScript allows this (the value becomes the `value` of the result with `done: true`); Velt doesn't because a finished `IteratorResult` carries no value; write `yield value;` before `return;` to produce a last value
generator_misuse.vlt:18:3: error: `yield` is only allowed in a generator function
declare the function with `function*` (methods: `*name()`) and the return type `Generator<T>`
generator_misuse.vlt:22:9: error: mismatched types
expected string, found f64
generator_misuse.vlt:26:3: error: `yield` needs a value of type `i64`
a bare `yield` is only allowed in a `Generator<void>`
generator_misuse.vlt:30:3: error: `await` is not allowed in a generator
a generator (`function*`) runs synchronously, one `next()` at a time: await the promise before calling the generator, or yield the promise for the caller to await
generator_misuse.vlt:38:5: error: `yield` cannot be used in a `finally` block
TypeScript allows this; Velt doesn't because a `finally` block also runs when the generator is closed early (`return()`, or dropping it), where it cannot pause; write the `yield` outside the `finally` block (at the end of the `try` block, or after the `try` statement)
generator_misuse.vlt:52:5: error: a `finally` block in a generator cannot throw, but this one may throw `Boom`
TypeScript allows this; Velt doesn't because the `finally` block also runs when the generator is closed early (`return()`, or dropping it), where an error has nowhere to go; write a `try`/`catch` inside the `finally` block that handles it
generator_misuse.vlt:58:5: error: `yield` is only allowed in a generator function
arrow functions cannot be generators: write a `function*` declaration (or a `*name()` method) and call it
generator_misuse.vlt:70:7: error: `break` cannot leave a `finally` block in a generator
TypeScript allows this; Velt doesn't because the `finally` block also runs when the generator is closed early (`return()`, or dropping it), where the generator must finish; write the loop inside the `finally` block, or move the `finally` code out of the loop
generator_misuse.vlt:84:9: error: `continue` cannot leave a `finally` block in a generator
TypeScript allows this; Velt doesn't because the `finally` block also runs when the generator is closed early (`return()`, or dropping it), where the generator must finish; write the loop inside the `finally` block, or move the `finally` code out of the loop
generator_misuse.vlt:91:13: error: generators cannot be created with `new`
write a generator function (`function* f(): Generator<T> { ... }`) and call it
